  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "description": "The proposed application seeks to modify the existing shopfront by replacing the current glass panels and entrance door with a new layout that features a centrally positioned door. The updated shopfront will be constructed with a aluminum frame, providing a clean and seamless appearance.\nAs part of the proposal, a roller shutter will also be installed for added security. The shutter box and guide rails will be discreetly concealed behind the fascia panel, ensuring the building’s architectural features remain unobstructed. In this case, the fascia panel forms part of a separate advertisement consent application submitted alongside this proposal.\nAdditionally, a mail slot is integrated into both the shutter and the glass door, ensuring functionality is maintained without compromising the overall aesthetic.\nThese proposed changes aim to enhance accessibility while maintaining a visually appealing and practical design that integrates seamlessly with the existing structure while also keeping in view the homogeneity of the proposed elements with the overall street scene.",
